  "name": "Brothers in Arms",
  "img": "/images/events/brothers-in-arms.png",
  "category": "solo",
  "description": "Also called KE. Points come only from killing enemy troops or losing your own troops, so it is one of the deadliest events.",
  "frequency": "Once a month, in the week of the normal Sunfire Castle battle.",
  "duration": "Friday 00:00 UTC to Sunday 00:00 UTC (2 days).",
  "phases": [
    {
      "name": "Start",
      "description": "Friday 00:00 UTC. The event begins and gatherings reset. The game gives 24 hours of notice."
    },
    {
      "name": "Sunfire Castle battle",
      "description": "The normal Sunfire Castle battle happens during the event window."
    },
    {
      "name": "End",
      "description": "Sunday 00:00 UTC."
    }
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Join the Sunfire Castle battle to gain points.",
    "Gathering during the event makes you a target. Check gatherings around alliances at the Friday 00:00 UTC reset.",
    "Attacking cities causes troop losses.",
    "Use a farm account or friendly battles if you do not want to take part.",
    "States usually set their own rules. Common ones: no attacks on cities in alliances in the top 5 or 10, attacks on gatherings are allowed until the Sunfire Castle battle is over, cities with no alliance or an alliance outside the top 5 or 10 can be attacked, and at most 2 attacks on each city. Ask your alliance leader.",
    "A failed attack loses 35% of the march (sent to the heaven), 10% injured (sent to the infirmary), and 55% lightly injured (back to the city).",
    "A failed defense injures 35% of your troops (infirmary) and lightly injures 65% (city). Troops over the infirmary capacity go to the Enlistment Office."
  ],
